# Frontend Rules (Next.js + TypeScript + Tailwind)

## Structure

- `app/`: routes and layouts only. `components/`: reusable UI. `lib/api.ts`: the single API
  client wrapper (base URL from env, attaches the token, normalises errors).
  `lib/auth.ts`: session/token handling. `types/`: shared types mirroring backend schemas.
- No `fetch` calls scattered through components; go through `lib/api.ts`.
- Components stay presentational where possible; put data fetching in page-level code or small
  hooks. No business rules in the UI (the server is the authority).
- TypeScript strict mode. No `any`; define types for API responses.
- Constants (labels, page sizes, route paths, role names) live in one place, not inline.

## Usability (graded: users have mixed digital literacy)

- Mobile-first, fully responsive; test at phone width first.
- Plain language, clear button labels ("Book this room", "I'm interested"), no jargon.
- A persistent home feed with tabs or chips for the main categories, a global search box, and
  the assistant reachable from every page (floating button or nav item).
- Emergency and schedule-change posts appear in a prominent banner at the top on every page.
- Every list has: loading skeleton, empty state with guidance, error state with retry.
- Every form has: inline validation (zod), disabled submit while sending, success and
  failure feedback, and preserves the user's input on error.
- Accessibility basics: labels on inputs, keyboard focusable controls, sufficient contrast,
  meaningful alt text, semantic headings.

## Role-aware UI

- Show or hide navigation and actions by role for convenience, but never rely on it for
  security. The backend enforces permissions.
- Staff dashboard: "my content", create/edit/archive, pending booking approvals, open
  requests, assistant insights (unanswered questions).
- Students: profile (faculty, year, programme) drives the personalised feed; make it easy to edit.

## Assistant UI

- Chat panel with message history, a typing indicator, and source chips that link to the
  cited content.
- Render suggested actions as buttons (e.g. "Open room booking").
- Show a clear message when the assistant is in fallback mode (search results only).
- Include thumbs up/down feedback on answers.

## Quality

- Format and lint before committing. No unused code or stray `console.log`.
- Keep dependencies minimal and log each new one in `DISCLOSURES.md`.
- Seed data must make every screen look populated for the demo.
